 "review": {"identity": "Devin SWE-2/swe2-max-1 (reviewer, fresh session context)", "method": "Acceptance suite run locally with `retail,gpu,audio` (CS_GAME_DIR, CS_ENGINE_IMAGE): the ignored windowed test drove the owner's own command `cs --cs-path $CS_GAME_DIR --mission M01 --smoke-seconds 45 --capture-dir private/evidence/F52-W2-evidence` on this machine's GPU (Apple M3 Pro, Metal). The smoke's presentation phase enqueued one labelled captioned test radio line (`smoke-probe`) on the production `RadioQueue` — voiced through `mix_radio` under the live bus levels, its start in `audio.one_shots` — pushed two designed `PlayerHit`s on the production `GameEventQueue`, and drove the live session's switches through the same `apply` the Preferences overlay uses: colour filter off then monochrome, cosmetic shake and flash kept then reduced, the subtitle row drawn then suppressed, UI scale 100% then 150%, the found session restored before the next phase. Every `presentation_probe_*` check judged the delivered frames; the four `frame_*_presentation_*.png` captures and `report.json` are hashed as artifacts, and each shot's record names the settings state its frame presented. The run is automated, never `human_play`, and no original executable ran; the probes and the flips are designed, not verified_original. This harness derives every field from the recorded log, production discovery of $CS_GAME_DIR, the smoke's report and the hashes of those artifacts. Validated with tools/validate_evidence.py --require-pass."},
 "claim": "implemented"
}
